"In the Mansion"
"The original purpose of this room is not at all easy to determine.  Splintered
bits of wood indicate that there was once a significant amount of furniture
here, but little decoration.  The large number of papers scattered about on
the floor, along with mud-stained ledgers make it likely that business was
once conducted in this room.  A single painting once hung on the dark wall,
and has left a dark outline.  The wood in one corner of the room looks a
little different from the rest of the bare planks.
